#: ../../plugins.rst:170
msgid "``plugin()`` is the public descriptor. ``load`` reads bounded UTF-8 configuration, checks its type and size, and allocates ``Settings`` in the session. The source hook checks expansion size before allocating. It replaces every marker, including markers inside code blocks; this is a text transformation, not a markup parser."
msgstr ""

#: ../../plugins.rst:175
msgid "The HTML hook escapes the label and inserts it before the last closing body tag. It uses ``assets_url`` supplied by the host, so nested pages link to the right CSS. This small example expects literal lowercase closing head and body tags. A plugin that rewrites arbitrary HTML should use a suitable parser and state its contract."
msgstr ""

#: ../../plugins.rst:180
msgid "The assets hook allocates its result array with ``ctx.allocator``. The CSS bytes are static. The SDK copies both paths and bytes into an owned result. Never return a slice pointing at a callback's local array. Session state must not retain hook inputs or hook-result allocations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../plugins.rst:185
msgid "The executable wrapper exposes the same descriptor over standard streams:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../plugins.rst:190
msgid "``serve_plugin`` handles negotiation and dispatch. Keep protocol output on stdout; write human logs to stderr. Return to ``main`` before ``os.exit`` so deferred cleanup runs. An embedded host instead passes the descriptor in ``project.Load_Options.plugins`` and selects its ID in the project's configuration."
msgstr ""

